│ "Efficacy and safety of a new clobetasol propionate 0.05% foam in Alopecia areata: A randomised, double-blind        │
│ placebo controlled trial. Abstract P08.17", "abstract": "Background  Clinical efficacy of topical corticosteroids in │
│ alopecia areata (AA) is still controversial. Positive clinical results have been obtained using ointments with       │
│ occlusive dressing but this approach has a low patient compliance. Recently, a new topical formulation (thermophobic │
│ foam: Versafoam®) of clobetasol propionate 0.05% has been introduced on the market (Olux®, Mipharm, Milan, Italy)    │
│ (CF). This formulation is easy to apply. After application to the skin the foam quickly evaporates without residues  │
